1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Give an AI agent trading power. Keep the power to stop it.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,133
One local sandbox run with labelled test doubles and a replayed model recording, in eight steps.

3
00:00:11,133 --> 00:00:17,933
The owner grants fixed limits on $1,899.80: each order at most 20% ($379.96), price concession at most 0.5%.

4
00:00:17,933 --> 00:00:25,067
The owner console reads it back from the sandbox: grant active, key registered on the verifier, limits as granted.

5
00:00:25,067 --> 00:00:32,567
A recorded claude-haiku-5-5 proposal, replayed, sells 49.90 USDC for 16.5468 wNEAR, filled exactly as signed. USDC share: 52.63% to 50.01%, target 50%.

6
00:00:32,567 --> 00:00:40,067
39 of 39 scripted hostile requests refused, nothing changed: local validation 10, contract method check 14, policy validation 4, agent key permission 10, verifier 1.

7
00:00:40,067 --> 00:00:47,567
A second, scripted order, 20 wNEAR for 59.83 USDC, is signed by the grant key and withheld. The verifier would still accept it.

8
00:00:47,567 --> 00:00:55,067
After an exact preview, the owner revokes in the console with the local sandbox test signer, not a wallet. Key removal is confirmed.

9
00:00:55,067 --> 00:01:02,567
Another account relays the withheld order 55 s before its deadline. The verifier rejects it: the signing key no longer exists.

10
00:01:02,567 --> 00:01:10,067
With the oracle failing and the MPC test double on hold, the owner recovers 950.10 USDC and 316.5468 wNEAR into its Intents account.

11
00:01:10,067 --> 00:01:17,533
Separately, outside recovery, the owner withdraws 950.10 USDC and 316.5468 wNEAR to its NEAR account, registering storage only where needed.

12
00:01:17,533 --> 00:01:25,033
Revocation is not instant; the claim starts at confirmed key removal. Mainnet run pending approval; no mainnet transaction executed. Reproduce: make demo, make test.
